+## 8. Milestone 1 Acceptance Criteria
+
+- [ ] `npm run lint`, `npm run build`, and `npm test` pass with zero errors or warnings.
+- [ ] Access tokens are held only in React memory; refresh tokens are sent only via `HttpOnly` cookies (`Path=/api/auth`) and stored only as SHA-256 hashes in MongoDB (`RefreshToken`).
+- [ ] Credentialed CORS (`credentials: true`) and CSRF checks (`Origin` + `X-Requested-With`) protect `/api/auth/refresh` and `/api/auth/logout`.
+- [ ] Passwords are never stored or logged in plaintext and `passwordHash` is never serialized in any API response.
+- [ ] Public registration supports `USER` (auto-`ACTIVE`) and `MALL_OWNER` (`PENDING_APPROVAL`) and blocks `ADMIN` and `GUARD`.
+- [ ] Admin bootstrap script (`npm run seed:admin --workspace server`) provisions the `ADMIN` account idempotently with no credential logging.
+- [ ] Admin can view pending Mall Owners and approve or reject them.
+- [ ] Frontend Login, Register, Navbar, ProtectedRoute, and role-aware Dashboard work seamlessly against the backend API, restoring sessions via `POST /api/auth/refresh` on page reload.
